From 9e7ba9c5818a08b49372dda2d2c4eac32096d641 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Janice <djanice1980@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:56:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: local -- no destructive FRL link test on a
 live link with an unchanged sink

Every link_detect() runs verify_link_capability(). For an FRL-capable HDMI sink the test is
destructive unless HDMI FRL is in use elsewhere or the sink carries the skip_frl_pre_training
panel patch: link_set_all_streams_dpms_off_for_link() commits dpms_off on the live stream, then
hdmi_frl_verify_link_cap() trains at the sink's maximum rate and disables the encoder output.

When the HPD pulse came from the same sink (same EDID), detection keeps the old dc_sink,
amdgpu_dm logs "dc_sink didn't change", and dm_restore_drm_connector_state() forces no commit
because the stream's sink still matches. The compositor answers the hotplug uevent with a commit
of the same mode, which is a fast update and leaves the stream dpms_off. The picture stays off
until a full modeset.

Measured with drm.debug=0x6 on an LG C2 (Max_FRL_Rate 6), 7.3.3, 2026-11-09 20:44: after a wake
the TV's receiver restarted (two trainings failed "FLT_READY not set by sink"), the TV then
pulsed HPD twice, each detection tested at 12G x4 and switched the stream off, KWin's commit
took 11 ms with no link enable, and the screen stayed dark for 4 minutes until a new modeset,
which trained 10G x4 and locked in 2 s. Same signature at 12:39 the same day.

Skip the destructive test when a stream on this link was created for the sink detection kept
and the link is active -- the condition the skip_frl_pre_training path already uses, plus the
sink check, for every sink. The earlier verified link cap still applies to that sink. A new or
changed sink, or a link with no active stream (cold plug, wake after the stream was removed),
still gets the full test.
---
 .../drm/amd/display/dc/link/link_detection.c   | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/link_detection.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/link_detection.c
index f254f2d..53c6af0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/link_detection.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/link_detection.c
@@ -995,6 +995,24 @@ static bool should_verify_link_capability_destructively(struct dc_link *link,
 					}
 				}
 			}
+		} else {
+			/*
+			 * Local: the same skip for every sink when the detection kept the
+			 * sink a live stream was created for (same EDID, so the earlier
+			 * test result still holds). The destructive test commits dpms_off
+			 * on that stream and disables the encoder, and with the sink
+			 * unchanged dm_restore_drm_connector_state() forces no commit, so
+			 * nothing turns the stream back on: an HDMI HPD pulse while the
+			 * picture is up (the LG C2 sends two while its receiver restarts
+			 * after a wake) left the screen dark until a full modeset.
+			 */
+			for (i = 0; i < MAX_PIPES; i++) {
+				if (pipes[i].stream != NULL &&
+						pipes[i].stream->link == link &&
+						pipes[i].stream->sink == link->local_sink &&
+						link->link_status.link_active)
+					destrictive = false;
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
